MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Aenima feels like a natural next choice after 10.000 Days because I want more of Tool's intricate rhythms and immersive songs. Indestructible similarly builds on my interest in Ten Thousand Fists and Disturbed's heavy, melodic hooks.",
    "The End of Heartache and Fury of Our Maker's Hand connect with my interest in In Flames and Soilwork through aggressive riffs, forceful grooves, and, especially for The End of Heartache, melodic vocals."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Stadium Arcadium and Into the Now miss what I want today: funk-influenced alternative rock and traditional hard rock do not satisfy my current appetite for heavier, modern metal.",
    "Same gives me too little information to identify the release or connect it to my listening, so I have no clear reason to choose it."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in rock seems to have been treated too broadly; sharing a rock connection does not mean an album offers the heaviness or rhythmic intensity I want now.",
    "My earlier interest in melodic hard rock seems to carry too much weight today. Crossfade fits that part of my listening, but it is less compelling right now than more Tool or heavier metal."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My latest listening to 10.000 Days and Ten Thousand Fists makes exploring more Tool and Disturbed particularly appealing right now.",
    "The particular combination of aggression, melody, and intricate rhythms matters more than heaviness alone: Mutter and Once More 'Round the Sun interest me, but I would choose the strongest connections to my recent listening first."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my taste for heavy, melodic music, but some give too much weight to broad rock similarities instead of my current interest in Tool, Disturbed, and aggressive metal with melody."
}
